    "result_text": "The build passes and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a `timezone` field on the owner response, derived from the region via a fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Timezone.java`** (new) \u2014 a pinned region-to-timezone table paralleling the existing `PostcodeRange`/`Locality` model tables. `Timezone.forRegion(region)` returns the IANA name (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`), or `null` for a region with no known timezone.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `timezone(owner)` derivation and its `@Mapping`. It reuses the existing `locality(owner)` region derivation rather than re-deriving from the postcode, so timezone and locality always agree: `Timezone.forRegion(locality(owner))`.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` property to the owner schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time).\n\nEach piece sits where it belongs: the lookup table in the model layer, the derivation in the mapper alongside the sibling `locality` mapping, and no logic duplicated. The acceptance test (`locality=NSW`, `timezone=Australia/Sydney`) passes; `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
